From f1760d5dfbc39bf47fcb6ba6d64158b41d5f6c55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Liu <kwliu@nuvoton.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:43:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: class: obmf: reset OBMF state on
 CLEAR_FEATURE(ENDPOINT_HALT)

The spec requires the device to flush its internal pipelines and reset
its counters when a STALL is cleared. Only the USB-layer RX buffer was
cleared; also notify the application through the bus_reset hook so it
drops fragment buffers and outstanding requests.

Reference: OCP OBMF-ICP over USB 1.0, Section 5 (Error recovery, CLEAR_FEATURE(ENDPOINT_HALT))
Signed-off-by: Joseph Liu <kwliu@nuvoton.com>
---
 subsys/usb/class/obmf.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/subsys/usb/class/obmf.c b/subsys/usb/class/obmf.c
index 6372cfb85bc..27eb1c521bd 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/class/obmf.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/class/obmf.c
@@ -405,12 +405,15 @@ static void obmf_status_cb(struct usb_cfg_data *cfg,
 	case USB_DC_CLEAR_HALT:
 		/*
 		 * [1.0rc5 C6] CLEAR_FEATURE(ENDPOINT_HALT) received.
-		 * Clear USB-layer RX buffer so the next transfer starts
-		 * cleanly. Upper-layer state cleanup is the application's
-		 * responsibility.
+		 * The device must flush its internal pipelines and reset its
+		 * counters, so clear the USB-layer RX buffer and have the
+		 * application drop its channel state like on a bus reset.
 		 */
-		LOG_WRN("Endpoint halt cleared: clearing OBMF USB-layer RX buffer");
+		LOG_WRN("Endpoint halt cleared: flushing OBMF state");
 		memset(obmf_buf, 0, sizeof(obmf_buf));
+		if (dev_data && dev_data->ops && dev_data->ops->bus_reset) {
+			dev_data->ops->bus_reset(common->dev);
+		}
 		break;
 	case USB_DC_SET_HALT:
 		LOG_WRN("Endpoint halt set");
